'''''Verbena incompta''''', the '''purpletop vervain''', is a species of [[plant]] from the [[genus]] ''[[Verbena]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Verbena incompta P.W.Michael |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/4086523 |access-date=2022-03-29 |website=www.gbif.org |language=en}}</ref> The species was described in 1995 by P.W. Michael.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Michael |first=Peter |date=1995 |title=A new name for a widespread and misunderstood species of Verbena |url=https://biostor.org/reference/249920 |journal=Telopea: Journal of Plant Systematics |volume=6 |pages=181–183 |via=biostor.org}}</ref>

The species is presumed to be of [[South America|South American]] origin, but also appears in [[Italy]] and [[Spain]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Verloove |first=Filip |date=2011-09-09 |title=Verbena incompta (Verbenaceae), an overlooked xenophyte in Europe |journal=Willdenowia |volume=41 |issue=1 |pages=43–49 |doi=10.3372/wi.41.41104 |s2cid=84693418 |issn=0511-9618|doi-access=free }}</ref>

